    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0294" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.6363 ST 2/120: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-04T17:00:00-04:00">May 4, 1937—5 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        6:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. Foreign Minister stated to me this afternoon: “We had to drive the Standard
                    Oil Company out of Bolivia for political reasons. It will never be allowed to
                    return”. This confirms last sentence my telegram No. 26.<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d301-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
